  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Defending the access of vulnerable groups to the Brazilian social security system</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will contribute to tackling inequality in Brazil by improving access to the Brazilian health and social security system of the most vulnerable. This will be done by building the interest and capacity of existing and new allies in local network organisations to monitor the implementation and resourcing of local health and social assistance policies. These organisations will be selected for their reach nationally and locally, and will include church pastoral networks and other groups with close contact with the poorest users of the health and social assistance systems. The project will bring national representatives of these networks together to influence debate about the social security system at national level, defending the rights of all citizens, especially the poorest, to health and social assistance policies that guarantee basic social rights. Spaces for social accountability of social security policies, particularly social assistance,  will be strengthened, so that the voices of service users and those representing their interests are present and  influence decision-making at local level.  

The project will also consolidate the resource mobilisation and financial management capacity of the partner, preparing Grito to apply for and potentially manage institutional funding to ensure future financial sustainability.</narrative>
  </description>
